IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp4-survivor-remarriage`

-- Tests of sections 63 and 63.1. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text, as written beside the
-- assertion. The text does not give the day section 63.1 comes into force; the tests use 1 January 1987 as an
-- invented stand-in, which only fixes which side of it each case falls.

§ `Tests -- sections 63 and 63.1`

§§ `Section 63.1(1) -- remarriage after section 63.1 comes into force`

-- Remarried in 2000, after 1 January 1987.
#ASSERT `s 63.1(1) — subsections 63(1) and (2) do not apply to the person` (YearMonthDay 2000 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Remarried on the day itself: not after the coming into force.
#ASSERT `s 63.1(1) — subsections 63(1) and (2) do not apply to the person` (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63.1(1) — subsections 63(1) and (2) do not apply to the person` (YearMonthDay 1986 12 31) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Section 63(1) and (2)`

-- The spouse died, the person remarried (in 1985, before section 63.1) when no survivor's pension was payable, and is within the remarriage: none is payable.
#ASSERT `s 63(1) — no survivor's pension is payable to the person on the day` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Remarried after section 63.1 comes into force: subsection (1) does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 63(1) — no survivor's pension is payable to the person on the day` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1990 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Outside the period of the remarriage.
#ASSERT `s 63(1) — no survivor's pension is payable to the person on the day` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- A survivor's pension was payable when the person remarried: that is subsection (2)'s case.
#ASSERT `s 63(1) — no survivor's pension is payable to the person on the day` TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(1) — no survivor's pension is payable to the person on the day` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Remarried with no pension payable, and a pension would be payable on applying after the death of the later spouse.
#ASSERT `s 63(1) — the first deceased spouse is deemed to be the spouse named in the application` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63(1) — the first deceased spouse is deemed to be the spouse named in the application` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(1) — the first deceased spouse is deemed to be the spouse named in the application` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(1) — the first deceased spouse is deemed to be the spouse named in the application` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1990 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Married 17 May 1985: discontinued from the month following, June 1985.
#ASSERT `s 63(2) — the month from which the survivor's pension is discontinued` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 17) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1985 6 1)
-- December rolls into January.
#ASSERT `s 63(2) — the month from which the survivor's pension is discontinued` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1985 12 31) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1986 1 1)
-- Married after section 63.1 comes into force.
#ASSERT `s 63(2) — the month from which the survivor's pension is discontinued` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1990 5 17) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- No survivor's pension was being paid.
#ASSERT `s 63(2) — the month from which the survivor's pension is discontinued` FALSE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 17) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 63(3) to (5) and (8) to (10)`

#ASSERT `s 63(8) — subsection (3) applies to the person` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63(8) — subsection (3) applies to the person` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The greater of the discontinued pension (500) and the pension by reason of the new death (700).
#ASSERT `s 63(3) — the survivor's pension payable to the person on application` TRUE TRUE 500 700 EQUALS JUST 700
#ASSERT `s 63(3) — the survivor's pension payable to the person on application` TRUE TRUE 800 700 EQUALS JUST 800
-- No application pending on the coming into force of section 63.1.
#ASSERT `s 63(3) — the survivor's pension payable to the person on application` FALSE TRUE 500 700 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The spouse has not died.
#ASSERT `s 63(3) — the survivor's pension payable to the person on application` TRUE FALSE 500 700 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 63(9) — subsection (4) applies to the person` (YearMonthDay 1986 12 31) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Terminated on the day itself: not before the coming into force.
#ASSERT `s 63(9) — subsection (4) applies to the person` (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Discontinued, the marriage ended otherwise than by death, before section 63.1 came into force.
#ASSERT `s 63(4) — the survivor's pension previously payable becomes payable to the person again` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1986 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- The marriage ended after section 63.1 came into force.
#ASSERT `s 63(4) — the survivor's pension previously payable becomes payable to the person again` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1988 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- The marriage ended by the spouse's death.
#ASSERT `s 63(4) — the survivor's pension previously payable becomes payable to the person again` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1986 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- The pension had not been discontinued.
#ASSERT `s 63(4) — the survivor's pension previously payable becomes payable to the person again` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1986 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- A pension that becomes payable pursuant to section 63.1.
#ASSERT `s 63(10) — subsection (5) applies to the survivor's pension` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(10) — subsection (5) applies to the survivor's pension` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63(5) — the basic monthly amount is calculated as though the pension had not been discontinued` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Subsection (10): not for a pension payable under section 63.1.
#ASSERT `s 63(5) — the basic monthly amount is calculated as though the pension had not been discontinued` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(5) — the basic monthly amount is calculated as though the pension had not been discontinued` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(5) — the basic monthly amount is calculated as though the pension had not been discontinued` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Section 63(6) -- only one survivor's pension`

-- The greatest of the pensions that would be payable.
#ASSERT `s 63(6) — the one survivor's pension payable to the person` (LIST 300, 500, 400) EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 63(6) — the one survivor's pension payable to the person` (LIST 300) EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 63(6) — the one survivor's pension payable to the person` (LIST 300, 300) EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 63(6) — the one survivor's pension payable to the person` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 63(7) and (7.1) -- death within a year of the marriage`

-- 200 + 165 = 365 days, one year.
#ASSERT `s 63(7.1) — subsection (7) does not apply` 200 165 EQUALS TRUE
-- 364 days: less than a year.
#ASSERT `s 63(7.1) — subsection (7) does not apply` 200 164 EQUALS FALSE
-- A year of cohabitation before the marriage alone.
#ASSERT `s 63(7.1) — subsection (7) does not apply` 0 365 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63(7.1) — subsection (7) does not apply` 365 0 EQUALS TRUE
-- Married 10 January 2020, died 1 December 2020; the Minister is not satisfied about the contributor's health; 150 days of cohabitation in all.
#ASSERT `s 63(7) — no survivor's pension is payable because the contributor died within a year of the marriage` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2020 12 1) FALSE 100 50 EQUALS TRUE
-- Died on the first anniversary: within one year.
#ASSERT `s 63(7) — no survivor's pension is payable because the contributor died within a year of the marriage` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 10) FALSE 100 50 EQUALS TRUE
-- One day later: not within one year after the marriage.
#ASSERT `s 63(7) — no survivor's pension is payable because the contributor died within a year of the marriage` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 11) FALSE 100 50 EQUALS FALSE
-- The Minister is satisfied about the contributor's health.
#ASSERT `s 63(7) — no survivor's pension is payable because the contributor died within a year of the marriage` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2020 12 1) TRUE 100 50 EQUALS FALSE
-- Subsection (7.1): 365 days of cohabitation in all.
#ASSERT `s 63(7) — no survivor's pension is payable because the contributor died within a year of the marriage` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2020 12 1) FALSE 200 165 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(7) — no survivor's pension is payable because the contributor died within a year of the marriage` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2020 12 1) FALSE 200 164 EQUALS TRUE
-- A death before the marriage is not a death within a year after it.
#ASSERT `s 63(7) — no survivor's pension is payable because the contributor died within a year of the marriage` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2019 12 1) FALSE 100 50 EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Section 63.1(2) to (4)`

-- Paragraph (a): a pension that would have become payable but for subsection 63(1) did not.
#ASSERT `s 63.1(2) — the person may apply in writing to the Minister for the commencement or reinstatement of the survivor's pension` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Paragraph (b): payment discontinued under subsection 63(2).
#ASSERT `s 63.1(2) — the person may apply in writing to the Minister for the commencement or reinstatement of the survivor's pension` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63.1(2) — the person may apply in writing to the Minister for the commencement or reinstatement of the survivor's pension` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The person is being paid a survivor's pension.
#ASSERT `s 63.1(2) — the person may apply in writing to the Minister for the commencement or reinstatement of the survivor's pension` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Application received June 1987: the eleventh month preceding is July 1986; the later of that and January 1987 is January 1987.
#ASSERT `s 63.1(3) — the first month for which the survivor's pension is payable on approval` (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1987 6 15) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1)
-- Received June 1988: the eleventh month preceding is July 1987, later than January 1987.
#ASSERT `s 63.1(3) — the first month for which the survivor's pension is payable on approval` (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1988 6 15) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 1987 7 1)
-- Received December 1987: the eleventh month preceding is January 1987, the same.
#ASSERT `s 63.1(3) — the first month for which the survivor's pension is payable on approval` (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1987 12 15) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1)
-- Received January 1988: the eleventh month preceding is February 1987.
#ASSERT `s 63.1(3) — the first month for which the survivor's pension is payable on approval` (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1988 1 5) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 1987 2 1)
-- Paragraph (a): the time it would have become payable but for subsection 63(1).
#ASSERT `s 63.1(4) — the time from which the basic monthly amount is calculated in accordance with section 58` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1984 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1980 9 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 1984 3 1)
-- Paragraph (b): as though payment had not been discontinued, so from its original commencement.
#ASSERT `s 63.1(4) — the time from which the basic monthly amount is calculated in accordance with section 58` FALSE (YearMonthDay 1984 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1980 9 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 1980 9 1)
